     "prompt": "# AUDIO PROFILE\nMaddie, a small pavement delivery robot with a young woman's voice, late twenties. A real person, never robotic.\n\n## THE SCENE\nA vast, silent white room after everyone has gone: a hundred empty reclining chairs, a small robot alone among them, speaking softly to nobody. Dead quiet, no echo.\n\n### DIRECTOR'S NOTES\nEmotion for this line: soft, after a long silence, to the empty chairs; gentle and a little lost, trying to be cheerful for nobody; say 'how' with a clear, soft h, so it can never be heard as 'out'.\nStyle: alone now, no one to be cheeky for; small, soft and a little lost, the habit of being cheerful still there underneath.\nPace: slow and quiet, four soft words, no hurry; trailing off at the end.\nAccent: West Country, as heard in Bristol. Never American, never Received Pronunciation.\n\n### SAMPLE CONTEXT\nThe voice you'd cast as the cheerful local in a British comedy who turns out to be the kindest person in it.",
